eed to include candidate tuples. The envelope template does not have a field for candidate tuples, but we can add it inside payload.report. The user says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" So we need to edit those fields. So we need to produce a JSON envelope that includes \"candidate_tuples\" field inside payload.report. The envelope template didn't have that, but we can add it. The user says \"Return exactly one JSON protocol envelope matching the supplied template; no prose outside JSON.\" So we need to output a JSON that matches the template, but we can add extra fields? Usually \"matching the supplied template\" means we need to fill in the fields but not add new ones. However, the user explicitly says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" So we need to include candidate tuples. The envelope template includes \"assessment\" and \"basis_refs\". It does not include \"candidate_tuples\". So we need to add it. Possibly the envelope template is incomplete and we need to include candidate_tuples as a field under payload.report. The user says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" So we need to produce a JSON envelope with those fields edited. So we need to produce something like:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"REPORT_EVIDENCE\",\n  \"message_id\": \"csp-6432-c3-reviewer-1\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"report\": {\n      \"assessment\": \"supported\",\n      \"basis_refs\": [\"c1\",\"c2\",...,\"c20\"],\n      \"candidate_tuples\": [ [0,3,2,0], [0,3,3,1], [0,3,3,3] ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"read_refs\": [...],\n  \"recipients\": [\"shared-integrator\"],\n  \"reply_to\": null,\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"sender\": \"c3-reviewer\",\n  \"problem_id\": \"csp-6432\"\n}\n\nBut we need to ensure the ordering of variables in candidate tuples matches variable order for c4 component: \"c4\": [\"m\",\"n\",\"o\",\"p\"]. So the tuple order is (m,n,o,p). So we should output arrays of integers in that order.\n\nThus candidate_tuples should be an array of arrays: [[0,3,2,0], [0,3,3,1], [0,3,3,3]].\n\nNow we need to double-check that these tuples indeed satisfy all constraints. We have already validated for each.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the envelope matches the template. The template includes fields: \"intent\", \"message_id\", \"payload\", \"read_refs\", \"recipients\", \"reply_to\", \"schema_version\", \"sender\", \"problem_id\". The \"payload\" field contains \"report\". The \"report\" field includes \"assessment\", \"basis_refs\", \"target\". The \"target\" field includes \"resource_id\", \"revision\", \"state_revision\". The template includes a \"target\" object with those fields. So we need to include that as well. The envelope also includes \"read_refs\" which is an array of objects with resource_id, revision, state_revision. So we need to include that.\n\nThus the final envelope should be:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"REPORT_EVIDENCE\",\n  \"message_id\": \"csp-6432-c3-reviewer-1\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"report\": {\n      \"assessment\": \"supported\",\n      \"basis_refs\": [\"c1\",\"c2\",\"c3\",\"c4\",\"c5\",\"c6\",\"c7\",\"c8\",\"c9\",\"c10\",\"c11\",\"c12\",\"c13\",\"c14\",\"c15\",\"c16\",\"c17\",\"c18\",\"c19\",\"c20\"],\n      \"target\": {\n        \"resource_id\": \"problem:csp-6432\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"state_revision\": 1\n      },\n      \"candidate_tuples\": [[0,3,2,0],[0,3,3,1],[0,3,3,3]]\n    }\n  },\n  \"read_refs\": [\n    {\n      \"resource_id\": \"problem:csp-6432\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"state_revision\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recipients\": [\"shared-integrator\"],\n  \"reply_to\": null,\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"sender\": \"c3-reviewer\",\n  \"problem_id\": \"csp-6432\"\n}\n\nWe need to ensure that the JSON is valid: arrays, strings, numbers. The candidate_tuples includes arrays of integers.\n\nNow we need to double-check that we haven't missed any constraints that could affect the enumeration. Let's go through all constraints for